## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to enforce data residency and leakage controls at runtime with low impact, using Vault for policy and identity, and blue/green rollouts for safe deployments.

## Key Concepts
- Data-loss prevention in containerized traffic
- Vault integration and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- Tenant-scoped JSON schemas
- Dynamic policy updates and hot-reload
- Canary/Blue-green deployment patterns

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal pseudo sidecar validator
const Validator = require('jsonschema').Validator;
const v = new Validator();
const tenant = process.env.TENANT_HEADER; // from request header
const schema = fetchVaultSchema(tenant); // resolves /secret/tenants/{tenant}/schema
v.addSchema(schema, '/tenant/schema');
const payload = getOutboundBody();
const result = v.validate(payload, { // simplified schema
  type: 'object', properties: { tenant: {type: 'string'}, data: {type: 'object'} }, required: ['tenant','data']
}, '/tenant/schema');
if (!result.valid) blockOrRedact(payload, result.errors);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test false positives/negatives per tenant?
- How would you handle schema evolution without breaking existing tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement data governance and privacy in a multi-DC setup: edge TLS, per-tenant policy, hot-reload, and observability with Loki, all integrated via docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- Traefik edge TLS termination across DCs
- Middleware-based response redaction per-tenant
- Docker Config hot-reload and policy delivery
- Loki-based centralized logs with per-tenant retention
- X-Tenant routing and impact on latency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express-style middleware skeleton for redacting response payloads per-tenant policy
function redactor(policy) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const oldSend = res.send;
    res.send = function (body) {
      let payload = typeof body === 'string' ? JSON.parse(body) : body;
      const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
      const p = policy[tenant] || { redact: [] };
      if (payload && typeof payload === 'object') {
        for (const key of p.redact) {
          if (payload.hasOwnProperty(key)) payload[key] = 'REDACTED';
        }
      }
      oldSend.call(this, JSON.stringify(payload));
    };
    next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test hot-reload correctness and no-downtime guarantees for policy updates?
- How would you measure and mitigate the performance impact of redaction on large payloads?
